== A. Anchors (textbook facts about the definitions, independent of the paper's claims)
H(Z) symplectic: True | det H = 1: True | I^2 = -1: True
squeeze diag(s, 1/s) symplectic: True
squeeze maps (1, K_ref) to (diag(s^2, s^-2), K_ref): Matrix([[s**2, 0], [0, s**(-2)]]) True
H-kinetic invariant under squeeze: True | K-kinetic invariant: True | V_lam invariant: True

== B. Is V_b invariant under the squeeze K -> S^-1 K S?  (finite transformation, sympy)
S^-1 K S = [[alpha, b/s**2], [c*s**2, -alpha]]
V_b(S^-1 K S) - V_b(K) = 2*alpha**2*mu*(-b + c*s**2)*(b + c*s**2)*(s - 1)*(s + 1)*(s**2 + 1)/((2*alpha**2 + b**2 + c**2)*(2*alpha**2*s**4 + b**2 + c**2*s**8))
V_naive(S^-1 K S) - V_naive(K) = 0  (the naive potential IS squeeze-invariant)
  K(phi=0.3) at H = 1 (compatible, V_lam = 0): det K = -1.00000; s = 2: V_lam 0 -> 0, V_b/mu -0.912668 -> -0.565450
  generic hyperboloid point alpha=0.8, b=0.5, c=0.72: det K = -1.00000; s = 2: V_lam 0.0121000 -> 0.0121000, V_b/mu -0.624878 -> -0.133472
  invariance set of the whole squeeze group: from the factored difference, alpha = 0 (where V_b = 0) or b = c = 0 (then alpha^2 = 1, K = +-K_ref)

== C. Continuous symmetries of V_b and of V_naive inside sp(2): solve dV(K + e[K, Xg]) = 0 for all K
V_naive: generators X = [[p, q], [r, -p]] with dV = 0 identically: [{q: 0, r: 0}]
V_b    : generators X = [[p, q], [r, -p]] with dV = 0 identically: [{p: 0, q: 0, r: 0}]

== D. The flat line: V_lam + V_b along (H = diag(y, 1/y), K = K_ref), and off it
V_lam(H(X, Y), K_ref) = X**2*lam/Y**2
V_total on (diag(y, 1/y), K_ref) = -mu
Cauchy-Schwarz anchor: Tr(K_ref^T K_ref) = 2 so V_b >= -mu, equality iff K parallel to K_ref

== E. Hessian at (1, K_ref) with lam = mu = 1
Hessian in my coords (X, Y, b, c): [[2, 0, -1, 1], [0, 0, 0, 0], [-1, 0, 3/2, -1/2], [1, 0, -1/2, 3/2]]
  gradient at the point: [0, 0, 0, 0]
  null space: [[0, 1, 0, 0]] (the Y direction = the squeeze line)
  in the documents' coords (x, y, u, t) the eigenvalues are {3 - sqrt(5): 1, sqrt(5) + 3: 1, 0: 1, 2: 1} = [0.0, 0.7639320225002103, 2.0, 5.23606797749979] (note v2 quotes 0, 0.764, 2, 5.236)

