== G. One-loop consequence in 1+1 (illustration): V_1 = (1/8pi) sum_i m_i^2 [1 + ln(L^2/m_i^2)] + const
The coefficient of ln(L^2) is (1/8pi) sum m^2; if it varies along the line, the classical flat
direction is lifted at one loop (no symmetry keeps it flat).
  y0 = 1: sum m^2 = 10.00000;  sum m^2 (1 - ln m^2) = -4.68986
  y0 = 2: sum m^2 = 14.50000;  sum m^2 (1 - ln m^2) = -13.98277
  y0 = 4: sum m^2 = 38.12500;  sum m^2 (1 - ln m^2) = -85.48193
